---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-universe.png";
import AssessmentPathway from "../components/AssessmentPathway.astro";
import CourseAtlas from "../components/CourseAtlas.astro";
import ListeningLab from "../components/ListeningLab.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
import "../styles/course.css";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="Radio telescope dishes beneath a measured night sky, with warm instrument light in the foreground"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <section class="course-intro" aria-labelledby="course-intro-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">A studio in accountable sonification</p>
      <h2 id="course-intro-title">Turn astronomical data into sound without hiding the translation.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>Students work like instrument builders: begin with a measured question, expose every operation, then test whether a listener can recover the intended pattern. Musical polish is welcome only after the evidence remains inspectable.</p>
    <dl>
      <div><dt>Level</dt><dd>Third-year studio</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Duration</dt><dd>12 weeks</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Prior audio</dt><dd>Not required</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Final work</dt><dd>Public listening instrument</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="course-thesis" aria-labelledby="thesis-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">The course position</p>
    <h2 id="thesis-title">Data does not sing by itself.</h2>
    <p>A telescope records measurements, not music. Every sound you make in this course must reveal its source, mapping and uncertainty, so a listener can tell what belongs to the universe and what belongs to your design.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="signal-chain-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">A repeatable method</p>
    <h2 id="signal-chain-title">The signal chain</h2>
    <ol class="signal-chain">
      <li><strong>Observe</strong><span>Find the measured quantity and its limits.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Map</strong><span>Choose what becomes pitch, time, timbre or space.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Listen</strong><span>Test what a listener can actually distinguish.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Disclose</strong><span>Publish the values, operations and uncertainty.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="atlas-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">The semester as one investigation</p>
    <h2 id="atlas-title">Twelve observations, one claim under pressure</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Each week changes the data object and the failure worth noticing. The signal chain stays visible, so techniques accumulate instead of resetting.</p>
    <CourseAtlas />
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="lab-preview-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Try the method before enrolling</p>
    <h2 id="lab-preview-title">Listening Lab: one curve, two mappings</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">The source stays fixed while one design decision changes. Listen, inspect the values, then decide which mapping supports the stated task.</p>
    <ListeningLab compact />
  </section>

  <section class="field-guide-callout" aria-labelledby="field-guide-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">A tool you keep</p>
      <h2 id="field-guide-title">The Sonification Field Guide</h2>
      <p>One reusable record for provenance, mapping, listening evidence and release checks. It follows every project from first values to public instrument.</p>
    </div>
    <a href={withBase("/field-guide/")}>
      <strong>Open the working method</strong>
      <span>Includes a downloadable Markdown template</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="assessment-path-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Assessment is the build sequence</p>
    <h2 id="assessment-path-title">Four submissions, one instrument</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Small mapping experiments become a signal study, then a critique, then a public work. Nothing is assigned only to be discarded.</p>
    <AssessmentPathway />
  </section>

  <nav class="course-switchboard" aria-label="Course areas">
    <a href={withBase("/lectures/")}><span>01</span><strong>Lectures</strong><small>Twelve questions and their observation guides</small></a>
    <a href={withBase("/sessions/")}><span>02</span><strong>{sessionLabels.plural}</strong><small>Weekly practice with an inspectable output</small></a>
    <a href={withBase("/lab/")}><span>03</span><strong>Open Listening Lab</strong><small>A complete mapping comparison in the browser</small></a>
    <a href={withBase("/policies/")}><span>04</span><strong>Policies and access</strong><small>Hearing safety, attribution and participation</small></a>
  </nav>
</ContentLayout>
